at":"2025-10-23T16:09:33Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111871","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111871","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111871.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111871.patch","merged_at":"2025-10-23T16:09:32Z"},"body":"Split from #110720\r\n\r\n- Pause active Android camera feeds on renderer pause and restore them on resume to avoid crashes when the OS tears down camera resources.\r\n- Refresh camera metadata and recompute feed rotation using the app’s reported orientation so front/back cameras stay correctly aligned after configuration changes.\r\n- Forward Android configuration orientation updates through `GodotLib.onScreenRotationChange()` and guard image callbacks with a mutex to keep metadata refresh and frame delivery synchronized.\r\n\r\nI wanted to split the rotation handling and lifecycle event handling, but both rely on refresh_camera_metadata(), so I couldn’t separate them.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nThis PR provides the following benefits:\r\n\r\n- Prevents camera preview crashes when auto-rotation is enabled.\r\n- Temporarily suspends camera functionality when the app is suspended to reduce battery consumption.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscription